<title>NETHERLANDS: Philips to shed 325 jobs at corporate HQ.</title>
<headline>Philips to shed 325 jobs at corporate HQ.</headline>
<dateline>EINDHOVEN, Netherlands 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philips Electronics NV said on Monday it would shed around 325 of the 730 jobs at its corporate centre in Eindhoven as part of a head-office restructuring announced in October.</p>
<p>A provisional plan had been submitted to the company's works council and trade unions on Monday, Philips said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;In future, the corporate centre is to focus on core strategic, financial and control functions, so as to improve the company's responsiveness and flexibility,&quot; Philips said.</p>
<p>Of the 325 jobs affected, 125 are to be transferred within the company, while an outsourcing scheme would cover a further 60, the company said. The remaining 140 workers will become redundant.</p>
